{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Py2h3uYm6SkogzsMBoPmGs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the workspace documents, here's what this project IS:\n\n- **It's John Liechty's \"Agentic Sandbox\" (Ghost World Labs / GWL)** â€” a research workspace at `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home` for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. It's explicitly a research project, not a production system; most of its ~80 root markdown files are design docs (whitepapers, plans, session logs), with a smaller set of runnable code.\n\n- **The shipping deliverable is the GWL master GUI** (`sandbox-lab-gui/`) â€” a custom Next.js + WebSocket app (`server.mjs`, launched via `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat` on port 3001) that launches and supervises agents running on the **OpenClaw** runtime (MIT-licensed, installed globally via npm). It pre-creates Gemini CLI, Claude Code, and Alpha-agent terminals and spawns more from an Agent Matrix.\n\n- **The daily-use agent vehicle is `alpha-v0`** â€” a general-purpose \"t2r\" (tasteâ†’reason) agent routed through a custom dispatcher (`brain/dispatcher/t2r-dispatcher.mjs`), defaulting to Gemini 3.1 Pro with a $100/month wallet cap, a 7-skill bundle, and per-project transcripts. Other agents (`alpha`, `sigma`, `prime-coder`, etc.) are research/legacy or planned-but-unbuilt, gated behind a toggle.\n\n- **The core research thesis is a \"brain\" architecture** â€” distill judgment from frontier models into small local students (QLoRA on â‰¤8B models, bounded by the gwl-server's RTX 4070 12 GB). It layers cognitive designs: Plain Vanilla Brain (PVB, live baseline), PVB+P (PoincarÃ© geometric memory, design-only), and FBB (hemispheric dialectic, further out).\n\n- **The current active engineering thrust is the \"Sovereign t2r harness\"** â€” a brain-agnostic agentic harness (clean ReAct loop, cache-stable tier routing, cost telemetry, MCP tools) intended to host three interchangeable brains: Opus-4.8 baseline, the efficient t2r brain, and a fully-local/air-gapped OSS brain. Per the most recent log (2026-06-09), a Crucible-forged, Foreman-ready multi-wave build plan exists in `plans/foreman/`, with harness-to-GA sequenced first.\n\n- **It ships supporting infrastructure too**: a master skill repo (`skills-master/`) linked into Claude/Gemini/OpenClaw, a canonical agent registry (`routing.json`), a Settings Vault for API keys, bootstrap tooling (`Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1`), and a large K-12 curriculum work product under `Curriculum/`.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from the documentation (CLAUDE.md, memory index, recent logs), not from re-reading the code itself this session. If you want, I can verify any specific claim â€” e.g., that `sandbox-lab-gui/server.mjs` and the t2r dispatcher actually exist and match the description."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6894,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20230,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20230},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b14e3af4-412b-438a-8779-832a3885cda2","uuid":"54b66777-13d7-47e0-8479-debc1c03656d","request_id":"req_011Cc38h7NdNCV5DjWvm5URh"}
